    <briefdescription>
<para>This is a compile-time <ref refid="dc/dd3/interfaceorg_1_1xvm_1_1asm_1_1_linker_context" kindref="compound">LinkerContext</ref> emulator, that is driven off of the information managed by the <ref refid="d7/d22/classorg_1_1xvm_1_1asm_1_1_assembler_context" kindref="compound">AssemblerContext</ref> <ndash/> and only that information! </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Specifically, it takes the conditions that have (for a given code path) already been tested (specified), and thus are known to be true. </para>
<para>For example, if a Module is marked as version 1 (using a <ref refid="d4/d43/classorg_1_1xvm_1_1asm_1_1constants_1_1_versioned_condition" kindref="compound">VersionedCondition</ref>) and the package under it is conditional on &quot;debug&quot; being defined, then the <ref refid="d7/d22/classorg_1_1xvm_1_1asm_1_1_assembler_context" kindref="compound">AssemblerContext</ref> at that point in the hierarchy implies a <ref refid="dc/dd3/interfaceorg_1_1xvm_1_1asm_1_1_linker_context" kindref="compound">LinkerContext</ref> that returns true for <computeroutput><ref refid="dd/d73/classorg_1_1xvm_1_1asm_1_1_simulated_linker_context_1a3fee8aa251dc191025da65c07dadb193" kindref="member">isSpecified(&quot;debug&quot;)</ref></computeroutput> and true for <computeroutput><ref refid="dd/d73/classorg_1_1xvm_1_1asm_1_1_simulated_linker_context_1a9e912625380d9b3a436e39d611b53432" kindref="member">isVersion(1)</ref></computeroutput> <ndash/> and returns true <bold><emphasis>only</emphasis></bold> for those two conditions! </para>
    </detaileddescription>
